3GPP TSG-RAN3 Meeting #102 R3-186581 Spokane, WA, USA, 12-16 November 2018 Title: [DRAFT] LS on PDU session split Release: Rel-15 Work Item: NR_newRAT-Core Source: Samsung [to be RAN3] To: SA2 Cc: Contact Person: Name: Hong Wang Tel. Number: E-mail Address: hong.wang@samsung.com Send any reply LS to: 3GPP Liaisons Coordinator, mailto:3GPPLiaison@etsi.org Attachments: R3-18xxxx 1. Overall Description: RAN3 has discussed the issues for PDU session split. RAN3 decides that NG-RAN can request the additional TNL information from the 5GC when the NG-RAN decides there are two NG-U tunnel terminations at the NG-RAN. The 5GC provides one additional UL TNL information per PDU session to the NG-RAN based on the request. A new class 1 message is defined in NG interface as in the attachment. In case the 5GC can not provide additional UL TNL information for the request PDU session, the NG-RAN can not setup two NG-U tunnel terminations per PUD session. 2. Actions: To SA2 ACTION: RAN3 kindly ask SA2 to take above into consideration. 3. Date of Next TSG-RAN3 Meetings: 3GPPRAN3#103 25 Feb - 1 Mar 2019 Athens GR 3GPPRAN3#103-Bis 8 - 12 Apr 2019 China CN

